      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "Fix failed automerge session reconciliation",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n- add `repair_failed` as an automerge terminal outcome when the linked repair workflow ends with `failure`, `timed_out`, or `action_required`\n- reconcile PR merged/closed state first, then validate the linked run repository, URL, and `repair-cluster-worker.yml` identity before terminalizing an open PR session\n- report failures best-effort from the repair workflow while keeping the seven-day scheduled reconcile as a fallback\n- expose the new outcome in the dashboard and include it automatically in terminal success-rate calculations\n- add single-session reconciliation, JSON output, help text, explicit exit codes, and conservative handling of invalid input or network failures\n\n## Root cause\n\nTerminal reconciliation only inspected the target PR's `merged_at` and `closed_at`. When the PR remained open but its linked repair workflow had already failed, the session stayed in `repairing` indefinitely and never entered the success-rate denominator.\n\n## Safety and behavior\n\n- merged and closed PR state takes precedence over repair-run conclusions\n- cancelled, neutral, skipped, successful, and in-progress repair runs do not map to `repair_failed`\n- successful requeue dispatches prevent the old session from being terminalized by the failed run\n- direct reporting and scheduled reconciliation use the same outcome-specific idempotency event ID\n- no KV migration or manual live data mutation is required\n\n## Validation\n\n- `pnpm run check`\n- `/data/code/openclaw/openclaw/.agents/skills/autoreview/scripts/autoreview --mode local --stream-engine-output`\n  - clean: no accepted/actionable findings\n",
